  "architecturalPlan": {
    "constructionScope": "exterior",
    "scaleRationale": "A 160 m² enclosed single-level villa is selected to give credible exterior envelope capacity for three bedrooms while keeping the tropical residence compact, calm and landscape-oriented; no budget or site dimensions were provided, so this is a design assumption rather than an area formula.",
    "levels": 1,
    "enclosedAreaM2": 160,
    "arrivalAndCirculation": "The public approach runs from the front arrival path to a recessed central entrance at the ground-floor walking datum of Y=0.20 m, while the private three-bedroom capacity is reserved behind the same protected envelope and service fit-out is deferred.",
    "volumeHierarchy": "A 16.0 × 10.0 m primary living-and-bedroom volume has a floor-top datum of Y=0.20 m, 3.40 m enclosure height and a thin flat roof at Y=3.72 m; the lower 12.0 × 5.0 m terrace canopy is deliberately subordinate at a 3.20 m underside datum.",
    "relationshipsAndViews": "The entrance faces the arrival court on the positive-Z side, broad garden-facing openings and the shaded terrace face the pool on the negative-Z side, and a continuous dry terrace-to-pool-deck route is held outside the water footprint.",
    "roofFacadeAndMaterials": "Warm ivory enclosure walls, bronze-framed glazed bays, timber shade posts and limestone pool paving establish a modern tropical palette, with deep flat roof edges, a freestanding terrace canopy, more open garden elevations and smaller side openings for shade and privacy.",
